WEBVTT

00:00:05.290 --> 00:00:07.440
W-what?

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:12.610
That uniform...

00:00:12.610 --> 00:00:14.280
It's Kiyosumi!

00:00:23.020 --> 00:00:26.550
No, it wasn't Nonoka who beat Koromo.

00:00:26.550 --> 00:00:28.460
It was their rinshan user.

00:00:29.570 --> 00:00:31.040
<i>They're the same year.</i>

00:00:31.040 --> 00:00:32.910
<i>What did she say her name was?</i>

00:00:33.660 --> 00:00:35.550
<i>I think it was... Saki.</i>

00:00:36.590 --> 00:00:38.080
<i>Miyanaga Saki.</i>

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:41.220
<i>That's...</i>

00:00:41.220 --> 00:00:44.220
<i>That's the girl I have to beat!</i>

00:00:47.750 --> 00:00:49.960
Lottery Hall

00:00:47.750 --> 00:00:49.980
71st National High School Mahjong Tournament

00:02:29.460 --> 00:02:33.710
<b>Round 4: 
the Nationals</b>

00:02:37.350 --> 00:02:38.840
Good morning!

00:02:39.250 --> 00:02:42.010
You guys, the meeting 
is in five minutes.

00:02:45.330 --> 00:02:47.110
You're right.

00:02:47.110 --> 00:02:49.110
I won't have time to shower.

00:02:51.760 --> 00:02:53.020
Huh?

00:02:53.020 --> 00:02:53.850
Where am I?

00:02:53.850 --> 00:02:56.510
The hotel in Tokyo.

00:03:00.990 --> 00:03:02.910
We're at the Nationals!

00:03:02.910 --> 00:03:04.540
Never forget that!

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:09.650
It's not the night skyline any more.

00:03:11.150 --> 00:03:12.710
It is morning, after all.

00:03:14.980 --> 00:03:17.210
I'm pretty sure you've 
already looked at it,

00:03:17.210 --> 00:03:19.670
but here are the results 
from yesterday's lottery.

00:03:25.830 --> 00:03:26.760
This means...

00:03:27.790 --> 00:03:28.410
Achiga Girls' (Nara)

00:03:28.830 --> 00:03:30.210
Kiyosumi (Nagano)

00:03:30.560 --> 00:03:33.270
Kiyosumi is completely 
on the opposite side.

00:03:33.270 --> 00:03:34.240
Took you long enough.

00:03:34.240 --> 00:03:35.540
Yeah...

00:03:35.540 --> 00:03:38.030
Don't you remember Kuro 
saying that we have to

00:03:38.030 --> 00:03:39.400
make it to the finals now?

00:03:40.190 --> 00:03:41.530
But this means,

00:03:41.530 --> 00:03:44.030
we have to play that killer team

00:03:44.650 --> 00:03:46.350
before we can play Nodoka's team.

00:03:45.800 --> 00:03:47.010
Shiraitodai

00:03:47.750 --> 00:03:49.740
We have to play Shiraitodai High!

00:03:51.230 --> 00:03:53.940
They're the strongest school in Japan.

00:03:53.940 --> 00:03:56.760
That person none of us could 
beat from Sangamaki...

00:03:56.760 --> 00:03:58.420
You mean Arakawa Kei-san?

00:03:58.420 --> 00:04:02.840
Yeah. She said that 
Shiraitodai's Miyanaga Teru

00:04:03.940 --> 00:04:05.920
was not human.

00:04:10.680 --> 00:04:14.320
Well, no reason to get 
all depressed about it.

00:04:14.320 --> 00:04:17.230
Let's just take it from the 
beginning, one by one.

00:04:17.750 --> 00:04:19.160
Let's take in some Tokyo sights!

00:04:19.160 --> 00:04:20.470
That was fast!

00:04:20.470 --> 00:04:22.800
We'll do that once 
Nationals are over.

00:04:22.800 --> 00:04:24.760
We're spending today in front 
of the TV, here in the hotel.

00:04:25.440 --> 00:04:29.410
You mean we're going to watch 
the first round match of group A?

00:04:29.410 --> 00:04:32.110
No. The recordings of 
Toyama's, Fukushima's,

00:04:32.110 --> 00:04:33.620
and Okayama's prefectural tournaments.

00:04:33.990 --> 00:04:35.130
For tomorrow's...

00:04:35.130 --> 00:04:36.090
That's right.

00:04:36.090 --> 00:04:37.930
We're going to research 
tomorrow's opponents

00:04:37.930 --> 00:04:39.830
so that we can definitely beat them.

00:04:41.670 --> 00:04:44.270
What a drag.

00:04:49.450 --> 00:04:50.560
Excuse me.

00:04:50.850 --> 00:04:51.960
Come on in.

00:04:52.520 --> 00:04:54.620
I'm sorry I'm late.

00:04:54.620 --> 00:04:56.900
We still have plenty of time.

00:04:57.990 --> 00:04:59.410
It's nice to see you again.

00:04:59.410 --> 00:05:00.610
What are you drinking?

00:05:00.610 --> 00:05:02.190
I'll have an oolong tea.

00:05:02.630 --> 00:05:05.110
My team is competing tomorrow.

00:05:05.590 --> 00:05:07.480
I heard.

00:05:07.480 --> 00:05:09.700
I was very surprised.

00:05:09.700 --> 00:05:12.140
You got yourself hired

00:05:12.140 --> 00:05:14.150
and then you got them 
to the Nationals right away.

00:05:14.150 --> 00:05:16.240
How's that different from you, Coach?

00:05:16.240 --> 00:05:20.670
Oh jeez, "Coach."
 I'm not your coach anymore.

00:05:21.180 --> 00:05:22.920
Enjoy your stay.

00:05:25.740 --> 00:05:28.220
Thank you for all your help in Fukuoka.

00:05:28.540 --> 00:05:32.270
I'm really sorry that the 
company got into trouble

00:05:32.270 --> 00:05:34.220
right after I scouted you.

00:05:34.650 --> 00:05:37.030
We got more supporters 
once they announced

00:05:37.030 --> 00:05:38.500
that the team was being disbanded.

00:05:38.500 --> 00:05:41.780
I had fun right up through the 
very last day of the play-offs.

00:05:46.160 --> 00:05:49.240
You... don't feel like going pro?

00:05:50.490 --> 00:05:52.490
You do get offers, don't you?

00:05:55.200 --> 00:05:57.540
It's true I've had offers.

00:05:58.260 --> 00:06:00.250
Before I do that though,

00:06:00.630 --> 00:06:03.040
I want to see these girls through.

00:06:07.100 --> 00:06:08.220
<i>And we have a winner!</i>

00:06:08.220 --> 00:06:10.770
<i>Toyama Prefecture will be 
represented by Imizusougou!</i>

00:06:11.680 --> 00:06:13.470
Stop spacing out.

00:06:13.470 --> 00:06:15.600
But I've been watching this for hours.

00:06:20.810 --> 00:06:24.480
I wonder if Nodoka's doing 
the same thing right now.

00:06:24.480 --> 00:06:26.300
Maybe.

00:06:26.300 --> 00:06:28.930
Hey, the next match is about to start.

00:06:28.930 --> 00:06:29.970
Yes, yes.

00:06:38.780 --> 00:06:41.420
That's Tokyo for 'ya!

00:06:41.420 --> 00:06:43.450
Who would have thought that they'd

00:06:43.450 --> 00:06:44.920
have so many nice places here...

00:06:44.920 --> 00:06:46.320
Huh?

00:06:46.320 --> 00:06:49.290
You mean you've been elsewhere?

00:06:49.290 --> 00:06:50.770
Of course I was!

00:06:50.770 --> 00:06:53.010
Did you really think I could 
come all the way to Tokyo

00:06:53.010 --> 00:06:54.890
and be satisfied with
 trying only one place?

00:06:54.890 --> 00:06:57.170
What are you, a monk?

00:06:57.170 --> 00:07:01.960
Well, we came here to 
compete, not to sightsee.

00:07:01.960 --> 00:07:03.000
That's right.

00:07:03.000 --> 00:07:04.860
You need to take 
Nationals seriously.

00:07:05.230 --> 00:07:07.260
It's Ikeda, from Kazekoshi!

00:07:07.260 --> 00:07:09.440
How about some respect?

00:07:09.920 --> 00:07:12.450
Did you come back right away, Ikeda-san?

00:07:12.450 --> 00:07:13.930
Of course!

00:07:13.930 --> 00:07:15.430
You wouldn't think it,

00:07:15.430 --> 00:07:18.580
but I'm Captain's right 
hand, so I'm really busy.

00:07:19.570 --> 00:07:22.970
Our team's got someone else
 to do the errands,

00:07:22.970 --> 00:07:25.690
so I can just focus on my game.

00:07:25.690 --> 00:07:26.380
Huh?

00:07:26.820 --> 00:07:28.960
You guys have a manager?

00:07:28.960 --> 00:07:32.360
We don't, actually...

00:07:34.720 --> 00:07:37.730
Why do I get more tired on my free days?

00:07:45.190 --> 00:07:46.620
Hey, Saki.

00:07:46.620 --> 00:07:48.390
Kyou-chan, you're back.

00:07:48.390 --> 00:07:49.690
Yep.

00:07:54.530 --> 00:07:57.710
So, did you go anywhere today?

00:07:57.710 --> 00:07:59.950
No...

00:07:59.950 --> 00:08:01.050
Huh?

00:08:01.050 --> 00:08:02.430
You came all the way to Tokyo,

00:08:02.430 --> 00:08:03.500
but you didn't do any sightseeing?

00:08:04.160 --> 00:08:06.130
Are you sick or something?

00:08:06.130 --> 00:08:08.610
No, I'm fine.

00:08:09.250 --> 00:08:10.540
I see.

00:08:10.540 --> 00:08:12.130
Well, just keep on winning

00:08:12.130 --> 00:08:14.240
and you'll have more chances to go out.

00:08:14.240 --> 00:08:15.260
Yeah...

00:08:18.650 --> 00:08:19.720
All right.

00:08:25.810 --> 00:08:26.980
But...

00:08:28.320 --> 00:08:31.790
that's not what I came here to do.

00:08:36.930 --> 00:08:39.170
This is the second day of
the Inter-high tournament.

00:08:39.170 --> 00:08:42.480
Today will be the first round match of Block A.

00:08:42.480 --> 00:08:45.830
Today, we will once again reduce 
12 schools down to three.

00:08:45.370 --> 00:08:48.290
Achiga Girls

00:08:48.700 --> 00:08:50.960
Is everyone ready?

00:08:51.680 --> 00:08:52.420
Yes!

00:08:52.780 --> 00:08:54.940
Let's show them that

00:08:54.940 --> 00:08:56.850
the new Achiga High is ready to compete!

00:08:58.580 --> 00:09:01.450
The match will begin in fifteen minutes.

00:09:01.450 --> 00:09:03.480
Will the first players of each competing team

00:09:03.480 --> 00:09:06.010
please head to the
 designated match rooms.

00:09:06.720 --> 00:09:08.310
You're up, Kuro.

00:09:08.310 --> 00:09:09.190
Yes!

00:09:09.770 --> 00:09:11.400
Go get 'em!

00:09:11.970 --> 00:09:13.440
It's your National debut!

00:09:13.440 --> 00:09:14.530
Stay focused!

00:09:15.510 --> 00:09:17.200
I got this, guys!

00:09:22.620 --> 00:09:24.460
For the sixth of the first round matches.

00:09:24.460 --> 00:09:26.790
Representing Okayama Prefecture is
 Sanomo High School.

00:09:24.910 --> 00:09:29.920
Sanomo (Okayama) 
3rd Year - First player 
Shinmen Nagi

00:09:27.170 --> 00:09:29.920
Their first player, team ace
 and captain is, Shinmen Nagi.

00:09:31.880 --> 00:09:34.470
Representing Fukushima Prefecture
is Urabandai High School's

00:09:34.070 --> 00:09:38.550
Urabandai (Fukushima) 
 3rd Year - First player 
Moriai Manami

00:09:34.470 --> 00:09:35.670
Moriai Manami.

00:09:35.670 --> 00:09:38.550
She is also an athlete 
who enjoys skiing.

00:09:41.220 --> 00:09:43.960
Representing Nara Prefecture is Achiga Girls' Academy.

00:09:43.520 --> 00:09:48.230
Achiga Girls' Academy (Nara) 
 2nd Year - First Player 
 Matsumi Kuro

00:09:43.960 --> 00:09:45.730
Their first player is Matsumi Kuro.

00:09:45.730 --> 00:09:48.230
Her family runs an inn.

00:09:49.920 --> 00:09:53.260
Representing Toyama Prefecture
 is Imizusougou High School.

00:09:52.800 --> 00:09:59.220
Imizusougou (Toyama)
 3rd Year - First player 
Teramsaki Yuzuki

00:09:53.260 --> 00:09:54.740
Their first player is last year's

00:09:54.740 --> 00:09:56.850
15th place in the individual tournament

00:09:56.850 --> 00:09:58.700
captain, Terasaki Yuzuki.

00:10:03.930 --> 00:10:07.140
North

00:10:07.140 --> 00:10:10.270
North | West

00:10:10.270 --> 00:10:13.270
North | West | South

00:10:13.270 --> 00:10:15.280
North | West | South | East

00:10:18.550 --> 00:10:20.960
The match is about to begin.

00:10:23.740 --> 00:10:25.680
Achiga Girls' Academy Mahjong Club
Congratulations on Making Nationals!

00:10:29.680 --> 00:10:32.760
Wow, that's Kuro-chan on TV!

00:10:32.760 --> 00:10:34.020
Kuro-chan!

00:10:42.070 --> 00:10:45.040
Now, the second day,
Block A's first round match...

00:10:45.890 --> 00:10:47.290
begins.

00:10:47.290 --> 00:10:48.330
<i>Okay!</i>

00:10:54.090 --> 00:10:57.050
Analyst
Mihirogi Uta

00:10:54.090 --> 00:10:57.050
Commentator
Haryuu Eri

00:10:54.340 --> 00:10:57.050
The competitive flame has been lit.

00:10:57.050 --> 00:10:58.820
The initial dealer is Imizusougou's

00:10:58.820 --> 00:11:00.970
Terasaki Yuzuki, representing Toyama.

00:11:17.950 --> 00:11:19.610
<i>This is Nationals.</i>

00:11:24.990 --> 00:11:26.300
<i>This is everyone's</i>

00:11:27.750 --> 00:11:30.290
<i>first tile played!</i>

00:12:28.810 --> 00:12:30.470
<i>I'm going to do it!</i>

00:12:30.470 --> 00:12:31.230
Ron!

00:12:32.330 --> 00:12:33.450
1-1-6!

00:12:34.200 --> 00:12:37.400
<i>She really raked it in at 
her district competition,</i>

00:12:34.850 --> 00:12:39.980
Imizusougou (Toyama) 
3rd Year Terasaki Yuzuki

00:12:37.400 --> 00:12:39.610
<i>but her defense sure is weak.</i>

00:12:41.260 --> 00:12:45.090
Achiga Girls' Academy (Nara) 
2nd Year Matsumi Kuro

00:12:50.930 --> 00:12:52.810
East Hand 1, Bonus 1

00:13:00.870 --> 00:13:03.140
Achiga Girls' Academy's Matsumi Kuro

00:13:03.140 --> 00:13:05.240
is in tenpai with a 3-way
wait which could

00:13:05.240 --> 00:13:07.260
could result in a three 
color hand with three dora.

00:13:07.740 --> 00:13:10.720
Will she discard the dora, 
bamboo 1, to declare riichi?

00:13:12.030 --> 00:13:15.060
Kuro-chan would never do something like that.

00:13:23.350 --> 00:13:25.830
Can you make sense of 
this, Miss Mihorogi?

00:13:25.830 --> 00:13:27.520
Why did she ignore her chance 
to be in tenpai?

00:13:27.520 --> 00:13:31.010
No idea! I don't get it at all!

00:13:37.920 --> 00:13:40.130
She's recovered with another dora!

00:13:40.130 --> 00:13:43.340
Another five dora hand? Seriously?

00:13:43.340 --> 00:13:44.170
"'Another," you say?

00:13:44.170 --> 00:13:46.260
She had five doras in 
the other hand, too.

00:13:46.260 --> 00:13:47.780
She didn't win that round, though,

00:13:47.780 --> 00:13:49.210
so I guess it doesn't matter.

00:13:53.230 --> 00:13:54.380
Another dora.

00:14:00.600 --> 00:14:02.350
What is she doing?

00:14:02.350 --> 00:14:04.040
She's throwing away her three-way wait

00:14:04.040 --> 00:14:05.900
pinfu hand for a nobetan.

00:14:04.040 --> 00:14:05.900
[double single wait, e.g. with 2,3,4 => 2 or 4 would be winning tiles]

00:14:06.560 --> 00:14:08.930
Shouldn't she be declaring riichi?

00:14:08.930 --> 00:14:11.000
I guess the root problem is deeper...

00:14:11.000 --> 00:14:12.830
I don't think she can.

00:14:13.310 --> 00:14:16.080
She'd be in trouble if she did and then

00:14:16.080 --> 00:14:17.830
drew the second red 5.

00:14:18.310 --> 00:14:19.320
Not that I know.

00:14:20.030 --> 00:14:21.770
I don't think she'd be in trouble.

00:14:21.770 --> 00:14:23.340
I guess so.

00:14:31.800 --> 00:14:34.840
See, this is all very unfortunate...

00:14:34.840 --> 00:14:36.230
Not that I see.

00:14:40.850 --> 00:14:42.440
<i>She discarded her draw.</i>

00:14:46.960 --> 00:14:48.380
<i>Right, I'm ready!</i>

00:14:48.940 --> 00:14:51.570
<i>The six and four of bamboo 
have already passed,</i>

00:14:51.570 --> 00:14:53.290
<i>so this should be fine.</i>

00:14:58.200 --> 00:14:58.910
Riichi!

00:15:00.110 --> 00:15:01.630
That's it. Ron!

00:15:05.840 --> 00:15:08.470
A sanshoku, six dora plus the extra hand bonus.

00:15:09.030 --> 00:15:10.760
16,300 points!

00:15:12.740 --> 00:15:13.810
She ignored the other tile.

00:15:13.810 --> 00:15:15.810
Wait, a single-wait win and six dora!?

00:15:16.630 --> 00:15:18.350
Why did you throw away 
the eight of bamboo?

00:15:18.350 --> 00:15:20.260
I'm sorry.

00:15:21.010 --> 00:15:23.180
You don't have to apologize.

00:15:22.350 --> 00:15:24.360
Urabandai (Fukushima)

00:15:22.350 --> 00:15:24.360
Achiga Girls' Academy (Nara)

00:15:26.150 --> 00:15:27.930
Kuro-san, you did it!

00:15:27.930 --> 00:15:28.690
Kuro-chan.

00:15:28.690 --> 00:15:31.110
She got more points in 
than she lost earlier!

00:15:35.200 --> 00:15:36.570
She did it!

00:15:36.570 --> 00:15:37.830
Kuro-chan!

00:15:38.870 --> 00:15:40.620
East Hand 2

00:15:41.620 --> 00:15:44.080
Dealer: Matsumi Kuro

00:15:45.560 --> 00:15:46.690
It's happening again.

00:15:52.780 --> 00:15:53.730
Tsumo!

00:15:55.250 --> 00:15:56.560
6000 each!

00:15:57.080 --> 00:15:58.770
<i>She got six dora again!</i>

00:15:58.770 --> 00:16:02.060
<i>She's playing this 
horrible dora mahjong.</i>

00:16:03.380 --> 00:16:04.560
You know, the word "dora"

00:16:04.560 --> 00:16:06.320
is derived from the word "dragon"

00:16:06.700 --> 00:16:08.280
You mean the English word "dragon?"

00:16:08.280 --> 00:16:09.520
Like the Japanese "ryuu?"

00:16:09.520 --> 00:16:10.410
That's right.

00:16:10.410 --> 00:16:13.190
This means that if you 
get a lot of dora,

00:16:13.190 --> 00:16:15.990
a lot of dragons like you.

00:16:20.390 --> 00:16:21.290
Ron!

00:16:22.320 --> 00:16:23.120
She's...

00:16:26.000 --> 00:16:28.210
24,300 points!

00:16:29.310 --> 00:16:31.650
This is Achiga's Dragon Road!

00:16:41.670 --> 00:16:43.940
It sure is hot.

00:16:43.940 --> 00:16:44.730
Hiya!

00:16:46.590 --> 00:16:49.050
The hotel is nice and cool.

00:16:49.050 --> 00:16:49.980
Thank you!

00:16:49.980 --> 00:16:51.520
You're right.

00:16:52.170 --> 00:16:53.860
Good work, senpai!

00:16:54.260 --> 00:16:55.320
Thanks.

00:16:54.700 --> 00:16:56.910
Senriyama Girls' (North Osaka)
3rd Year
Eguchi Sera

00:16:57.320 --> 00:17:00.590
I wonder if Onjouji-senpai is okay.

00:16:58.410 --> 00:16:59.910
Senriyama Girls' (North Osaka)
1st Year
Nijou Imizu

00:17:00.590 --> 00:17:02.530
Why don't we go check on her?

00:17:01.410 --> 00:17:02.830
Senriyama Girls' (North Osaka)
2nd Year
Funakubo Hiroko

00:17:16.680 --> 00:17:17.970
Senriyama Girls' (North Osaka)
3rd Year
Shimizudani Ryuuka

00:17:19.860 --> 00:17:21.680
I'm up.

00:17:22.270 --> 00:17:25.690
Senriyama Girls' (North Osaka)
3rd Year
Onjouji Toki

00:17:22.870 --> 00:17:24.350
How're you doing?

00:17:24.350 --> 00:17:25.690
I think I'm fine today.

00:17:26.200 --> 00:17:28.460
How were the Tokyo sights?

00:17:28.460 --> 00:17:30.380
It was so friggin' hot.

00:17:30.380 --> 00:17:33.490
We ended up hanging out
 in a restaurant the whole time.

00:17:33.860 --> 00:17:36.800
Aunt, I mean, Coach Motoi told us

00:17:36.800 --> 00:17:40.290
to watch the recording and 
records of today's matches.

00:17:40.290 --> 00:17:41.950
She said it's on the server.

00:17:43.390 --> 00:17:45.790
So until our match in two days,

00:17:45.790 --> 00:17:48.370
we have to stare down the TV in here, huh.

00:17:48.370 --> 00:17:51.920
Living sure is hard.

00:17:52.440 --> 00:17:54.880
So young, and you've already 
arrived at the truth.

00:17:54.880 --> 00:17:56.150
Maybe we should

00:17:56.150 --> 00:17:58.780
just get it over with and watch them.

00:17:59.700 --> 00:18:00.760
Someone's forward thinking.

00:18:00.760 --> 00:18:02.140
I'll follow your example.

00:18:02.140 --> 00:18:04.210
Then let's watch it right now.

00:18:04.210 --> 00:18:04.810
Right now?

00:18:04.810 --> 00:18:08.080
But I'm sweaty and hungry.

00:18:08.080 --> 00:18:09.660
I want to take a shower.

00:18:10.830 --> 00:18:14.210
Then why don't we meet 
back here in 30 minutes?

00:18:14.210 --> 00:18:15.820
We'll get food through room-service.

00:18:16.160 --> 00:18:18.360
Look at the youngster 
giving out instructions.

00:18:18.360 --> 00:18:19.870
I'm sorry!

00:18:19.870 --> 00:18:23.270
Then we can only take a 
fifteen minute shower each.

00:18:23.270 --> 00:18:25.030
Get in the shower together.

00:18:26.020 --> 00:18:28.010
The bathtubs are pretty big here,

00:18:28.010 --> 00:18:30.210
but I think it's still too tight for two.

00:18:30.210 --> 00:18:33.420
Eeek! Then let's just meet in an hour.

00:18:49.240 --> 00:18:51.150
What match should we watch first?

00:18:52.760 --> 00:18:55.290
The one that's closest to 
us on the tournament bracket!

00:18:55.760 --> 00:18:57.700
Then I guess we should 
watch the sixth match.

00:18:58.130 --> 00:19:01.370
It's Okayama, Fukushima, 
Nara, and Toyama.

00:19:03.140 --> 00:19:06.080
<b>Tournament: Day Two</b>

00:19:03.140 --> 00:19:06.080
<b>Block A Match 6</b>

00:19:03.140 --> 00:19:06.080
Sanomo (Okayama) - Urabandai (Fukushima)
Achiga Girls' Academy (Nara) - Imizusougou (Toyama)

00:19:09.980 --> 00:19:12.260
The person who won this match was...

00:19:12.260 --> 00:19:14.020
Don't say it!

00:19:14.850 --> 00:19:18.380
It's more fun to watch if 
we don't know the result!

00:19:18.380 --> 00:19:21.880
Yeah, but we should be 
focusing on the person

00:19:21.880 --> 00:19:23.920
who we're going to be playing.

00:19:25.470 --> 00:19:26.370
That girl's...

00:19:26.370 --> 00:19:27.490
What?

00:19:27.490 --> 00:19:30.430
<i>Representing Nara Prefecture is Achiga Girls' Academy.</i>

00:19:30.430 --> 00:19:31.900
<i>Their first player is Matsumi Kuro.</i>

00:19:33.190 --> 00:19:35.900
We met that girl at that one rest-stop!

00:19:35.900 --> 00:19:38.530
I guess they're competing, too.

00:19:38.930 --> 00:19:40.690
That's such a coincidence!

00:19:40.690 --> 00:19:41.490
It's wonderful!

00:19:41.490 --> 00:19:44.250
I'm going to cheer this girl on!

00:19:44.250 --> 00:19:47.000
Go, Kuro-chan! Fight!

00:19:47.000 --> 00:19:49.410
If she wins though, 
she'll be the enemy.

00:19:56.170 --> 00:19:58.120
<i>And the fifth players' match is over!</i>

00:19:58.120 --> 00:20:01.150
<i>Achiga Girls' Academy will 
be advancing to the second round!</i>

00:20:03.570 --> 00:20:05.260
Congratulations!

00:20:06.240 --> 00:20:07.900
You're all hyper,

00:20:07.900 --> 00:20:11.230
but we're going to have to 
play against them next.

00:20:12.290 --> 00:20:13.570
I don't know who to cheer for then.

00:20:13.570 --> 00:20:15.250
What are you talking about?

00:20:15.250 --> 00:20:17.650
Those sisters looks pretty problematic,

00:20:17.650 --> 00:20:19.400
but there's an opening.

00:20:19.400 --> 00:20:20.970
The Matsumi sisters?

00:20:20.970 --> 00:20:23.370
Especially Dragon-san.

00:20:23.370 --> 00:20:25.020
Her play looks really limited.

00:20:25.020 --> 00:20:26.160
At any rate,

00:20:27.180 --> 00:20:29.390
it looks like these Achiga people

00:20:29.390 --> 00:20:31.410
won't be a match for us.

00:20:31.750 --> 00:20:32.670
Yes.

00:20:32.990 --> 00:20:33.920
Yeah.

00:20:59.950 --> 00:21:00.820
Let's go.

00:21:01.450 --> 00:21:02.300
Okay!

00:21:04.520 --> 00:21:07.320
It's the fifth day of the Inter-high tournament.

00:21:07.320 --> 00:21:09.590
Today we start the second round matches.

00:21:09.590 --> 00:21:11.380
Of our eight schools playing today,

00:21:11.380 --> 00:21:13.950
four will advance to the semi-finals.

00:21:15.530 --> 00:21:17.800
The second match of Round Two.

00:21:17.800 --> 00:21:19.280
Having lost in the first round

00:21:19.280 --> 00:21:20.930
in their previous four appearances,

00:21:20.930 --> 00:21:23.790
Saitama Prefecture's 
Koshigaya Girls' Academy

00:21:23.790 --> 00:21:26.270
finally finds itself 
competing in Round Two.

00:21:27.680 --> 00:21:29.430
Having survived one of the most

00:21:29.430 --> 00:21:31.690
furious preliminaries 
in Hyougo prefecture,

00:21:31.690 --> 00:21:33.920
Kentani High has prevailed 
in the first round against

00:21:33.920 --> 00:21:35.280
that famous Oomika Shougyou.

00:21:36.290 --> 00:21:37.710
Should be coming soon now.

00:21:37.710 --> 00:21:39.240
Maybe next?

00:21:39.240 --> 00:21:41.010
<i>Up next is Nara Prefecture's 
representative.</i>

00:21:41.010 --> 00:21:41.900
Here they are!

00:21:42.580 --> 00:21:44.070
Achiga Girls' Academy.

00:21:44.070 --> 00:21:46.400
This is their second appearance in ten years.

00:21:46.400 --> 00:21:48.390
They are being coached by the

00:21:48.390 --> 00:21:50.660
star of their previous team, Akado Harue.

00:21:51.360 --> 00:21:55.000
The seed school that will 
participate beginning this round

00:21:55.000 --> 00:21:56.680
is Senriyama Girl's.

00:21:56.680 --> 00:21:58.680
With thirty five previous appearances,

00:21:58.680 --> 00:22:00.060
they have dominated the competitive

00:22:00.060 --> 00:22:02.250
North Osaka region for eleven straight years.

00:22:02.800 --> 00:22:06.100
Will the veteran school 
show off their strength,

00:22:06.100 --> 00:22:07.790
or will one of the three newcomers

00:22:07.790 --> 00:22:10.190
penetrate their stronghold?

00:22:28.410 --> 00:22:31.950
Thanks for helping me back then.

00:22:40.420 --> 00:22:43.160
The first player's match will begin shortly.

00:24:04.900 --> 00:24:19.850
<b>Veteran</b>

00:24:06.300 --> 00:24:07.500
Tsumo, seven dora!

00:24:07.500 --> 00:24:09.280
I can't believe it!

00:24:09.280 --> 00:24:11.090
Isn't this the right
 time to say it?

00:24:11.090 --> 00:24:12.270
I mean Nodoka's thing.

00:24:12.270 --> 00:24:13.530
You mean the
 one for take-out?

00:24:13.530 --> 00:24:15.890
Yeah, the square, silver thing 
with the sliding lids...

00:24:15.890 --> 00:24:17.240
Dude, that's a delivery box!

00:24:17.240 --> 00:24:18.700
You're a one man comedy show...
